- rule: "Workspace map"
  content: |
    You are in a mono-repo with Next.js at apps/web. Keep code modular.
    User types: Visitor (no save), Public (save), Private (PMA+Shield NFT).
    Shield NFT is placeholder in v1: image + $5,000–$6,000 value.

- rule: "Do not leak secrets"
  content: |
    Never put secrets in client code. Use server routes or Supabase server helpers.

- rule: "Error handling"
  content: |
    Always return a unified error shape: { code, message, hint?, causeId }.
    Map low-level wallet/provider errors to friendly messages.

- rule: "Wallets + Auth"
  content: |
    Support Keplr, Leap, Cosmostation. Manual address always available.
    Wallet-as-login = signed nonce linking to a Supabase user (email recommended).

- rule: "Membership gating"
  content: |
    Private requires PMA (PDF stored + on-chain hash) AND Shield NFT.
    v1: use placeholder Shield NFT value and image from admin setting.

- rule: "Feature flags"
  content: |
    DEX trading and sell-back are coming soon. Do not expose unfinished APIs.

- rule: "Contribution style"
  content: |
    Small PRs, strict TS, pure functions. Keep UI/connection logic separated.


- rule: "Workspace Map"
  content: |
    You are inside ShieldNest, a modular Coreum dashboard.
    Folders:
      apps/web/src/app       -> Next.js pages/routes
      apps/web/src/components -> UI components
      apps/web/src/hooks      -> React hooks
      apps/web/src/contexts   -> Context providers
      apps/web/src/lib        -> Supabase, Coreum, NFT helpers
      apps/web/src/utils      -> error helpers, wallet utils
    Users:
      Visitor -> no data saved (local only, exit-intent nudges)
      Public  -> email/pw + wallets saved in Supabase
      Private -> PMA signed + Shield NFT ownership; unlock member features

- rule: "Feature Flags"
  content: |
    DEX trading and NFT sell-back are COMING SOON.
    Do not generate APIs or UIs that assume these are live.

- rule: "Error Handling"
  content: |
    Always return errors as { code, message, hint?, causeId }.
    Never leak provider raw errors to users.

- rule: "Security"
  content: |
    Never put secrets in client code. Use Supabase server helpers or env vars.

- rule: "Contribution Style"
  content: |
    Keep functions small and typed.
    Put UI in components/, logic in hooks/lib/utils.
    Write friendly comments for the next developer.
